xnu 0231: does the render backend write memory at all?

Every write measured so far is the CP's: the canary, the fence, the RPTR
shadow. The self test's clear, texel upload and draw all read black, and with
glcopy=0 the layer surface the panel scans stays all zero while the CP's own
writes land in the same boot, so the question is whether the RB's stores reach
DRAM at all.

RB_DONE_TS (event 22) is emitted by the RB pipeline itself and writes a 64-bit
timestamp only with WRITE_ENABLED set (`adreno_pm4.xml`, CP_EVENT_WRITE7). The
test puts one in an IB with a fence behind it and polls the address: a nonzero
timestamp says the engine that draws can write memory, zeros say it cannot, and
the two point at different halves of the port.

Boot argument gprbdone=1.
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -72,6 +72,8 @@
 static int mondrian_uc_frame_logged;
 static uint32_t mondrian_uc_pm4;
 static int mondrian_uc_noblit;
+/* gprbdone=1: ask the RB for its own timestamp (0231). */
+static int mondrian_cp_test_rbdone;
